WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:04.362
Start with a real business process: meeting follow-up.

2
00:00:04.362 --> 00:00:09.665
We turn scattered inputs into a controlled workflow, then make every result easy to review.

3
00:00:10.065 --> 00:00:14.992
Use Gemini to structure the meeting notes, then put the decision record in Word.

4
00:00:14.992 --> 00:00:18.996
In Excel, separate decisions, open questions, owners, and dates.

5
00:00:18.996 --> 00:00:22.568
A summary becomes useful when responsibility is explicit.

6
00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:25.403
Connect the approved actions in n eight n.

7
00:00:25.403 --> 00:00:30.679
Check the incoming record, assign the owner, and branch overdue items into a review queue.

8
00:00:30.679 --> 00:00:34.447
Keep the original meeting reference attached to every follow-up.

9
00:00:34.847 --> 00:00:39.820
The same checked data becomes a Word brief, a PowerPoint summary, and an email draft.

10
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:45.378
A shared dashboard makes team action dashboard visible, with an owner and a clear next action.
